    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Relation</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">refine</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le_antisymm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?_</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Relation</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">reflTransGen_idem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Relation</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">reflTransGen_idem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 584765497,
        "sender_full_name": "Bolton Bailey",
        "timestamp": 1775859330
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Is there a similar theorem about <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Order/Closure.html#ClosureOperator\">ClosureOperator</a> maybe? (seems <a href=\"https://loogle.lean-lang.org/?q=%E2%8A%A2+%28%3Fa+%3A+ClosureOperator+%3Fb%29+_+%3D+%28%3Fa+%3A+ClosureOperator+%3Fb%29+_\">no</a>)</p>",
        "id": 584765822,
        "sender_full_name": "Bolton Bailey",
        "timestamp": 1775859548
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well all we're using here is that <code>ReflTransGen</code> is <code>Monotone</code> and idempotent, so instead of adding a bunch of these for <code>ReflGen</code> and <code>TransGen</code> etc we could just add these two in the general form <code>a ≤ b → b ≤ f a → f a = f b</code> and <code>a ≤ f b → b ≤ f a → f a = f b</code> for a monotonic idempotent <code>f</code></p>",
        "id": 584766071,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1775859733
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, I guess ClosureOperator also has this extensive property which is not needed here. But then, it's still the case that the various <code>Gen</code>s could be made members of that structure, so if we didn't want to write out all the implications in the lemma statement we could write <code>eq_of_le_of_le</code> for that structure, or make a finer-grained structure for just the monotone and idempotent properties.</p>",
        "id": 584766651,
        "sender_full_name": "Bolton Bailey",
        "timestamp": 1775860068
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hmm it might be nice to add an <code>IsIdempotent</code> class, or an <code>Std.Idempotent</code> to core (they have the unrealted <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Std.IdempotentOp#doc\">docs#Std.IdempotentOp</a>)</p>",
        "id": 584766698,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1775860102
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For the sake of recording keeping: this weekend I realized this was already in CSLib as <a href=\"https://api.cslib.io/docs/find/?pattern=Relation.reflTransGen_mono_closed#doc\">cslib#Relation.reflTransGen_mono_closed</a> (added by none other than me last year <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span>). The proof there is:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Relation</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reflTransGen_mono_closed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r₁</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">ext</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">ReflTransGen</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">reflTransGen_closed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which I think is more direct in using what's in Mathlib already.</p>",
        "id": 603014779,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1781423874
    }
]